  "program_text": "program 11 INTL - International Studies World Languages and Culture COAA_World Languages and Culture Go Back Print Certificate of Achievement-Advanced (COA-A) World Languages and Culture New Online Option Noncredit New for Spring 2026 Program Description Pending state approval. Please check with the CTE Division Office for status. The Certificate of Achievement-Advanced in World Languages and Culture provides students with the opportunity to strengthen their multilingual abilities and deepen their understanding of multicultural perspectives. This foundation equips them to effectively engage with non-English-speaking communities in the Bay Area, as well as in global contexts such as international travel, law, business, and nonprofit or nongovernmental organizations. This certificate demonstrates high beginner proficiency (above Level 2) in two world languages. Given De Anza College’s richly diverse and multilingual community, the program supports students by offering a formal path to expand their language skills and cultural knowledge. Understanding linguistic and cultural diversity offers a critical lens through which to view global and local issues, making this certificate an excellent complement to undergraduate or graduate studies in fields such as Anthropology, History, Law, Chicanx Studies, Linguistics, or Business. In addition to fulfilling the transfer language requirement, the Certificate of Achievement-Advanced in World Languages and Culture enhances students’ academic and professional profiles, particularly for careers in civil service, international work, or the private sector. Program Learning Outcomes Upon completion, students will be able to Demonstrate the ability to engage in communicative tasks that require describing personal experiences in the present with some references to the past; expressing basic opinions about issues of relevance in one´s life; understanding main ideas and supporting details in aural and written discourse; producing discourse-level writing related to one´s life experiences Demonstrate an understanding of the diversity of cultural, historical, and regional contexts of the peoples and cultures of the world Analyze constructions of cultural and social differences (as expressed through language) while examining one´s own cultural positionings and assumptions De Anza College Requirements Noncredit Certificate Requirements Each course listed as a program requirement must be completed with a C grade, passing grade or satisfactory progress Each course must be completed at De Anza College Skills Certificate Requirements Skills Certificates are awarded by departments and are not notated on official college transcripts. Contact the department directly for assistance in applying for a skills certificate. Completion of all major courses with a C grade or higher Each course must be completed at De Anza College Certificate of Achievement Requirements Certificates of Achievement are awarded by the college and notated on official transcripts. Each course listed as a program requirement must be completed with a letter grade of C or higher. Pass/No Pass grades are not accepted for these courses. No more than six quarter units may be transferred from other academic institutions Certificate of Achievement-Advanced Requirements Certificates of Achievement-Advanced are awarded by the college and notated on official transcripts. Each course listed as a program requirement must be completed with a letter grade of C or higher. Pass/No Pass grades are not accepted for these courses. Students must demonstrate proficiency in English and Mathematics by qualifying for ENGL C1000, ENGL C1000H or ESL 5, and by qualifying for MATH 114 or a transfer-level Math course No more than 18 quarter units may be transferred from other academic institutions Cal-GETC Certificate of Achievement-Advanced Requirements See Cal-GETC pattern found at deanza.edu/articulation/ge-requirements . Note: This is an exception to the Certificate",
